(FIL-91: a dynamic buffer grows to hold a file far larger than any initial reserve, with no error flag and no truncation.
 Also covers: FIL-85, FIL-90, FIL-97.
 80000 bytes into a buffer that started at capacity 4096. Note the first
 line: the manual (LANGUAGE.md:3816) says a dynamic buffer starts at zero
 capacity; it reports 4096. That is the buffers ledger's Discrepancy 1,
 restated by this section's own text - see FIL-90.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-91.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   4096
   80000
   80000
   80001
